's it so eat your meals the same  time every day you know in Silicon  Valley the better company you are the  more food they serve during the day it's  the opposite you won't work or  productivity work or health short term  and long term same time every day for  meals for when you get up and when you  go to bed and you'll have an impact on  your own performance and so my message  today really is about empowerment it's  that human health is something that we  all have within us and the opportunity  to get we all have to know ourselves  though you know when I was doing the PR  for one of the books I went on a talk  show remotely from Australia and one of  the rules we have a book called short  guide to a long life which is 56 rules  of to do's and not to Do's so in the  middle of the interview the the guy says  you know one of your rules says that you  have to get naked and look at your body  once a month in a mirror I say yes you  have to know your body and your butt I  was going through all that and then they  shift to the other anchor and she's  naked how was that and they had a camera  on my face because apparently nudity is  allowed on Australian television and my  face was shocked and they just wanted to  see the reaction of America into nudity  but I'm a believer that you're each in  charge of your own health in today's  world we have technology where you can  measure anything the notion that you  show up at your doctor at one o'clock  and he or she says your blood pressure  is okay whoever checked in the morning  when you get up at night when you go to  bed when you're pissed off after a phone  call with enough data arrow goes away  and so you are in charge of your own  health and so the reason I write these  books the reason I do CBS News is to  push people in the right direction  because it's an obligation on my side to  educate and teach and really hopefully  together we can achieve a better health  outcome so it's a privilege to be here  today and we're so excited to see the  dedication to the book thank you very  much  and now from the Rancho Mirage writers  festival in California
 

